  <section>
    <h2>Quick Answer</h2>
    <p>The 28th China Hi-Tech Fair (CHTF) will be held in Shenzhen from <strong>November 26–28, 2026</strong>, at the <strong>Shenzhen World Exhibition &amp; Convention Center in Bao'an District</strong>.</p>
    <p>If you are coming from outside China, there are three things to sort out before your trip:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Register for CHTF.</li>
      <li>Make sure you can enter Mainland China.</li>
      <li>Plan how you will get to the exhibition center.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>CHTF preregistration is free if completed before <strong>12:00 noon on November 25, 2026</strong>. The official ticket notice says registration after that deadline costs <strong>RMB 120</strong>.</p>
    <p>Some international visitors may also be able to attend CHTF using China's <strong>240-hour visa-free transit policy</strong> instead of obtaining a Chinese visa in advance. This can be especially useful if Shenzhen is one stop in a trip that continues to Hong Kong or another country or region.</p>
    <p class="cta"><a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">Check your itinerary with the Jadebound 240-hour transit checker →</a></p>
  </section>

