  <section>
    <h2 id="transit">Can You Attend CHTF Using 240-Hour Visa-Free Transit?</h2>
    <p>Possibly.</p>
    <p>China's 240-hour visa-free transit policy currently covers travelers from <strong>57 countries, including the United States, United Kingdom, Canada, Australia and many European countries</strong>. Short business visits are permitted under the policy, so attending a trade fair such as CHTF can fit the permitted activities. See the <a href="https://en.nia.gov.cn/n147418/n147463/c183412/content.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">current NIA policy</a> and <a href="https://en.nia.gov.cn/n147418/n147468/c217849/content.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">nationality update</a>.</p>
    <p>The easiest way to understand the route requirement is:</p>
    <p><strong>Country or region A → Mainland China → different country or region B</strong></p>
    <p>For example:</p>
    <p class="table-hint">On narrow screens, scroll the route table sideways to read both columns.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap route-table" role="region" aria-label="CHTF transit route examples" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Example route</th><th scope="col">Transit route requirement</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>U.S. → Shenzhen → Hong Kong</td><td>Route can qualify</td></tr>
          <tr><td>U.S. → Shenzhen → Japan</td><td>Route can qualify</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hong Kong → Shenzhen → Singapore</td><td>Route can qualify</td></tr>
          <tr><td>U.S. → Shenzhen → U.S.</td><td>Does not qualify for the transit route requirement</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Those examples only show how the route rule works. Your passport, entry port, onward booking and other requirements still need to qualify.</p>
    <p>For the full eligibility requirements, see our:</p>
    <p class="cta"><a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/">China 240-Hour Visa-Free Transit Guide</a><br />or <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">check your itinerary with the Jadebound transit checker</a>.</p>
    <p>U.S. passport holders are currently among the eligible nationalities. For more U.S.-specific information, see <a href="/do-us-citizens-need-a-visa-for-china/">Do U.S. Citizens Need a Visa for China?</a></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="hong-kong">Combining Shenzhen and Hong Kong</h2>
    <p>Shenzhen's location next to Hong Kong makes CHTF particularly convenient for travelers who want to combine the fair with a Hong Kong visit.</p>
    <p>Hong Kong can count as the country or region before or after Mainland China for the 240-hour transit route requirement.</p>
    <p>For example:</p>
    <p><strong>U.S. → Shenzhen → Hong Kong</strong></p>
    <p>can meet the route requirement because you enter Mainland China from the United States and leave Mainland China for Hong Kong.</p>
    <p>But:</p>
    <p><strong>U.S. → Hong Kong → Shenzhen → Hong Kong → U.S.</strong></p>
    <p>does not meet the route requirement. For your Mainland China visit, you arrived from Hong Kong and returned to Hong Kong.</p>
    <p>This is why your flight or train connections matter — not just the country where your overall trip begins and ends.</p>
    <p>If you plan to travel from Shenzhen to Hong Kong, have your confirmed Shenzhen-to-Hong Kong travel arrangements ready before entering China. Your later Hong Kong-to-U.S. flight is a separate part of the trip.</p>
    <p>The <a href="https://english.shanghai.gov.cn/en-Visa2/20251020/b6d40e72778f4ea1a83a20f4664341d4.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Shanghai government FAQ on London → Shanghai → Hong Kong</a> confirms Hong Kong's role in a qualifying route. For complete eligibility requirements, current entry ports and stay rules, see our <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/">China 240-Hour Visa-Free Transit Guide</a>. See also the <a href="https://en.nia.gov.cn/n147418/n147463/c183412/content.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">current NIA policy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="arrival-port">Flying Into Shenzhen Under the 240-Hour Policy</h2>
    <p>For most international visitors flying directly to CHTF, <strong>Shenzhen Bao'an International Airport</strong> is the most straightforward arrival point and is currently an eligible port under the 240-hour policy.</p>
    <p>Travelers arriving from Hong Kong by train, ferry or land crossing should check their exact entry point before booking because the list of eligible Guangdong ports has changed over time.</p>
    <p>See our <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/">China 240-Hour Visa-Free Transit Guide</a> for the current list of eligible entry ports.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="registration">How to Register for China Hi-Tech Fair 2026</h2>
    <p>CHTF recommends registering before the event.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to the <a href="https://www.chtf.com/english/Info/ForVisitors/Notice/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official CHTF visitor registration page</a>.</li>
      <li>Complete the registration form and questionnaire using your real identity information.</li>
      <li>Use the same passport details you will travel with.</li>
      <li>Save the electronic badge/QR confirmation after your registration is approved.</li>
      <li>Bring your original passport to the exhibition.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The <a href="https://www.chtf.com/english/Info/ForVisitors/First/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official English visitor guide</a> says approved visitors can enter throughout the three-day event and instructs international visitors to use their passport for entry.</p>
    <p>If you have trouble registering with an overseas phone number or passport, contact CHTF rather than guessing how to complete the form.</p>
    <p>Visitor enquiry:<br /><strong><a href="mailto:sarah@zhenweiexpo.com">sarah@zhenweiexpo.com</a></strong><br /><strong>WhatsApp: +86 15130613049</strong></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="tickets">Register Before November 25 to Avoid the RMB 120 Fee</h2>
    <p>The official 2026 CHTF ticket notice says:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Complete preregistration before <strong>12:00 noon on November 25</strong>: free admission.</li>
      <li>Register after the deadline: <strong>RMB 120</strong>.</li>
      <li>Ticket registration closes at <strong>3:00 PM on November 28</strong>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The English CHTF pages do not currently repeat the RMB 120 fee information. See the <a href="https://www.chtf.com/canguanzhiyin/gonggao/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official CHTF 2026 ticket notice (Chinese)</a>.</p>
    <p>The page can be translated into English using Chrome. Recheck the official notice before registering in case the rules change.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="admission">What Should International Visitors Bring to CHTF?</h2>
    <p>International visitors should bring:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>their <strong>original passport</strong></li>
      <li>their <strong>electronic badge or QR confirmation</strong></li>
      <li>any China visa or entry documents required for their trip</li>
    </ul>
    <p>CHTF's English pages describe both <a href="https://www.chtf.com/english/Info/ForVisitors/Notice/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">passport scanning</a> and <a href="https://www.chtf.com/english/Info/ForVisitors/Admission/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">QR-code entry</a>. These instructions are not necessarily contradictory, so having both your original passport and electronic confirmation is the simplest approach.</p>
    <p>If the scanner does not accept your passport or QR code, ask for assistance at the <strong>Overseas Visitors / visitor service desk</strong>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="children">Traveling With Children? Check With CHTF First</h2>
    <p>The official 2026 CHTF pages currently give conflicting information about visitors under 16.</p>
    <p>The <a href="https://www.chtf.com/english/Info/ForVisitors/Admission/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">English admission page</a> says visitors must be above 16. The <a href="https://www.chtf.com/canguanzhiyin/ruchangxuzhiX/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chinese admission page (Chinese)</a> says visitors under 16 are not admitted. However, the <a href="https://www.chtf.com/canguanzhiyin/gonggao/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official Chinese ticket notice (Chinese)</a> says children under 16 may enter free with a guardian after signing an on-site waiver.</p>
    <p>Because these instructions conflict, do not rely on any one of them when planning an international trip.</p>
    <p><strong>Contact CHTF directly before bringing anyone under 17.</strong></p>
    <p>Visitor enquiry:<br /><a href="mailto:sarah@zhenweiexpo.com">sarah@zhenweiexpo.com</a><br />WhatsApp: +86 15130613049</p>
    <p>Visitors over 70 are also advised by CHTF to attend with an accompanying adult and valid admission.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="invitation-letters">Do You Need a CHTF Invitation Letter?</h2>
    <p>If you need an invitation letter for a Chinese visa application, CHTF provides an official invitation-letter process.</p>
    <p>The CHTF website instructs visitors to:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Download the official invitation template.</li>
      <li>Complete the requested information.</li>
      <li>Email it to <strong><a href="mailto:sarah@zhenweiexpo.com">sarah@zhenweiexpo.com</a></strong>.</li>
      <li>CHTF can sign and stamp the invitation.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>See the <a href="https://www.chtf.com/english/Info/ForVisitors/visaInformation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official English CHTF Visa Information page</a>.</p>
    <p>An invitation letter does not guarantee that a Chinese visa will be issued. CHTF also does not publish a guaranteed processing time, so request the letter well before your visa appointment.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="venue">Where Is China Hi-Tech Fair Held?</h2>
    <p>CHTF 2026 will be held at:</p>
    <p><strong>Shenzhen World Exhibition &amp; Convention Center (Bao'an)</strong><br />No. 1 Zhancheng Road<br />Fuhai Street, Bao'an District<br />Shenzhen, China</p>
    <p>Chinese address:</p>
    <p><strong lang="zh-CN">深圳市宝安区福海街道和平社区展城路1号</strong></p>
    <p>Do not confuse Shenzhen World Exhibition &amp; Convention Center in Bao'an with the older Shenzhen Convention &amp; Exhibition Center in Futian. They are different venues in different parts of Shenzhen.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="airport-transport">Getting to CHTF From Shenzhen Bao'an Airport</h2>
    <p><strong>Shenzhen Bao'an International Airport (SZX)</strong> is the most convenient airport for the exhibition center.</p>
    <p>The venue's <a href="https://www.shenzhen-world.com/overview/traffic/en/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official transportation information</a> places Shenzhen World about <strong>7 km from Terminal 3</strong>.</p>
    <h3>By Metro</h3>
    <p>From Shenzhen Airport Terminal 3:</p>
    <p><strong>Line 11 → Airport North → transfer to Line 20 → Shenzhen World</strong></p>
    <p>For the South Lobby:<br />use <strong>Shenzhen World Station</strong>, Exit C1 or C2.</p>
    <p>For the North Lobby:<br />use <strong>Shenzhen World North Station</strong>, Exit C1 or C2.</p>
    <p>Metro Lines <strong>12 and 20</strong> both serve the exhibition center. See the <a href="https://www.sz.gov.cn/en_szgov/life/transport/metro/content/post_12870342.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Shenzhen government Metro information</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="hong-kong-airport">What If You Fly Into Hong Kong?</h2>
    <p>Hong Kong International Airport may offer better flight options for some international travelers, but reaching CHTF from Hong Kong adds a border crossing.</p>
    <p>If you are relying on the 240-hour visa-free transit policy, decide how you will enter Mainland China <strong>before booking your Hong Kong transfer</strong>, because your Hong Kong → Shenzhen route becomes part of your immigration itinerary.</p>
    <p>See <a href="#hong-kong">Combining Shenzhen and Hong Kong</a> and <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">check your itinerary with the Jadebound transit checker</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="hotels">Where Should You Stay?</h2>
    <h3>Near Shenzhen World / Bao'an</h3>
    <p>This is the easiest choice if CHTF is the main purpose of your trip. Look for a hotel near Shenzhen World or a convenient Line 12/20 Metro station.</p>
    <p>When booking, verify that the hotel is near <strong>Shenzhen World Exhibition &amp; Convention Center in Bao'an</strong>, not the convention center in Futian.</p>
    <h3>Nanshan or Futian</h3>
    <p>Nanshan and Futian can make sense if you also have business meetings or sightseeing elsewhere in Shenzhen, but your daily trip to CHTF will be longer.</p>
    <p>Check the Metro route before booking rather than choosing a hotel based only on the word “Shenzhen.”</p>
    <h3>Staying in Hong Kong</h3>
    <p>Hong Kong is better treated as another stop on the trip than as a daily CHTF base.</p>
    <p>Crossing the border every morning and evening adds time and immigration formalities. If you are using 240-hour visa-free transit, leaving Mainland China also ends that particular entry, so do not assume you can simply cross back and forth under the same permission.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="checklist">CHTF 2026 Travel Checklist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Register for CHTF before November 25 at noon if possible.</li>
      <li>Save your electronic badge/QR confirmation.</li>
      <li>Bring your original passport.</li>
      <li>Confirm whether you need a Chinese visa or can use a visa-free policy.</li>
      <li>If using 240-hour transit, <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">check your complete route with the Jadebound checker</a>.</li>
      <li>Confirm the exact Mainland China entry point if arriving from Hong Kong.</li>
      <li>Save the venue's English and Chinese addresses.</li>
      <li>Check which exhibition hall you need before choosing a Metro station or hotel.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <details><summary>When is China Hi-Tech Fair 2026?</summary><p>China Hi-Tech Fair 2026 will be held November 26–28, 2026 in Shenzhen.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where is CHTF 2026?</summary><p>At Shenzhen World Exhibition &amp; Convention Center in Bao'an District, not the convention center in Futian.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is CHTF registration free?</summary><p>The official 2026 ticket notice says preregistration completed before 12:00 noon on November 25 is free. Registration after that deadline costs RMB 120. Recheck the official notice before registering.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I attend CHTF without a Chinese visa?</summary><p>Possibly. Travelers who qualify for a Chinese visa-free entry policy may not need to obtain a visa in advance. Eligible travelers whose itinerary meets the 240-hour visa-free transit rules may also be able to attend CHTF during their transit stay. See our <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/">China 240-Hour Visa-Free Transit Guide</a> or <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">use the Jadebound transit checker</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I fly to Shenzhen and then go to Hong Kong?</summary><p>For eligible 240-hour transit travelers, a route such as U.S. → Shenzhen → Hong Kong can meet the route requirement. Your passport, entry port, onward booking and other requirements still need to qualify.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does Hong Kong → Shenzhen → Hong Kong qualify for 240-hour transit?</summary><p>No. You would be entering Mainland China from Hong Kong and returning to Hong Kong, so the country/region immediately before and after Mainland China would be the same.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What should I bring to enter CHTF?</summary><p>International visitors should bring their original passport and their electronic badge/QR confirmation.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can children attend CHTF?</summary><p>The official 2026 CHTF pages currently give conflicting rules for visitors under 16. Contact CHTF directly before bringing anyone under 17.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can CHTF provide a visa invitation letter?</summary><p>Yes. CHTF publishes an invitation template and asks visitors to email the completed form for an official signature and stamp. The invitation does not guarantee visa approval.</p></details>
  </section>

